  SOLUTION - 
  DELETE p1
FROM Person p1 INNER JOIN Person p2
WHERE p1.email=p2.email AND p1.id>p2.id


Pyspark solution  - 
from pyspark.sql.types import *
from pyspark.sql.functions import *
from pyspark.sql.window import Window
from pyspark.sql import SparkSession

spark = SparkSession.builder.appName("Delete Duplicate Emails").getOrCreate()

window_spec = Window.partitionBy("email").orderBy(col("id").desc())

# Create a new DataFrame with a row number for each partition
df_with_rownum = df.withColumn("row_num", row_number().over(window_spec))

# Filter the DataFrame to keep only the unique rows based on the row number
df_unique = df_with_rownum.filter(col("row_num") == 1).drop("row_num")

# Show the resulting DataFrame
df_unique.show()



